  "desk_commentary": {
    "newbuilding": "continued to \nflow this week;\n\nIn the tanker sector, Greek owner \nLatsco Shipping reportedly placed an \norder for 2x 115,000 dwt tankers at \nSK Oceanplant for around USD 77 \nmillion \neach, \nwith \ndeliveries \nscheduled for June and November \n2030, with options retained for two \nmore.\n\nIn the container sector, Chinese \nowner China United Lines placed an \norder \nfor \n2x \n14,000 \nteu \ncontainerships at Hudong-Zhonghua \nfor around USD 150 million each, \nwith \ndeliveries \nscheduled \nfor \nDecember 2028.\n\nThe vessels will be conventionally \nfuelled.\n\nGreek owner Akrotiri Tankers also \nplaced an order for 1x 157,000 dwt \nSuezmax tanker at New Times \nShipyard for around USD 84.4 \nmillion, with delivery scheduled for \nJune 2029.\n\nGreek \nowner \nNavios \nMaritime \nPartners reportedly placed an order \nfor \n4x \ncontainerships \nat \nHJ \nShipbuilding for around USD 122.7 \nmillion \neach, \nwith \ndeliveries \nscheduled for December 2027.\n\nThis brings the owner's total order to \ntwo Suezmax tankers.\n\nNo teu capacity has been confirmed \nat this stage.\n\nSwiss/Turkish \nowner \nAdvantage \nTankers \nreportedly \nordered \n4x \n157,000 dwt Suezmax tankers at",
    "secondhand": "Another active week in the second-\nhand market, with a number of \ntransactions reported across both the \ndry bulk and tanker sectors.\n\nTsuneishi changed hands for around \n$17 mln.\n\nIPSEA COLOSSUS 59,000 dwt 2011 \nKawasaki was reportedly sold for \naround \n$20.75 \nmln, \nwhile \nYC \nAEQUOR 57,000 dwt 2012 Ningbo \nBeilun Lantian Shbldg changed hands \nfor high $13 mln.\n\nIn the dry bulk sector, HC WISDOM \n96,000 dwt 2013 Imabari Shbldg was \nreportedly sold for around $24.5 mln, \nwhile LC MILADY 94,000 dwt 2011 \nShanghai \nWaigaoqiao \nShbldg \nchanged hands for high $14 mln.\n\nThe sister vessels NEW LIULINHAI \n56,000 dwt 2004 Nantong COSCO KHI \nShip Eng and PLACID SEA 56,000 dwt \n2004 Nantong COSCO KHI Ship Eng \nwere reportedly sold for around $10 \nmln each.\n\nThe sister vessels RTM FLINDER \n90,000 \ndwt \n2013 \nNamura \nShipbuilding and RTM DIAS 90,000 \ndwt 2013 Namura Shipbuilding were \nreportedly sold for around $21.4 mln \neach.\n\nPUTERI SEJATI 48,000 dwt 2002 \nOshima was sold to Chinese interests \nfor around $6.1 mln.\n\nAmong the Kamsarmax vessels, GCL \nHAZIRA 82,000 dwt 2021 Nantong \nCOSCO KHI Ship Eng was sold to \nEuropean interests for high $38 mln, \nwhile NEW WAVELET 82,000 dwt \n2021 Nantong COSCO KHI Ship Eng \nchanged hands for around $42 mln.\n\nCELESTE 34,000 dwt 2012 Zhejiang \nJingang Shipbuilding was sold to \nGreek interests for around $11.1 mln, \nwhile IVS KESTREL 33,000 dwt 2014 \nKanda Kawajiri changed hands for \naround $17 mln.\n\nBABITONGA \n82,000 \ndwt \n2019 \nTsuneishi Holdings - Fukuyama was \nsold to Sincere Navigation for around \n$38.5 mln.\n\nIn \nthe \ntanker \nsector, \nSEAKING \n319,000 dwt 2013 Hyundai was \nreportedly sold to ADNOC for around \n$177 mln, while VADIN 302,000 dwt \n2006 Mitsui Chiba Ichihara changed \nhands, still to ADNOC, for around \n$117 mln.\n\nFurther down the sizes, GOOD HOPE \nMAX 77,000 dwt 2005 Sasebo was \nreportedly sold for mid $12 mln, \nwhile GENEVA STAR 76,000 dwt 2009",
    "demolition": "The status quo continues across the \nIndian \nSub-Continent \ndemolition \nmarkets which remains starved of \nfresh tonnage. \nDespite strong improvements in \nscrap prices post monsoon season - \ncharter markets across all sector \ncontinue to keep Owners happy and \nlooking anywhere but the sub \ncontinent as their next destination. \nMore locally, the Pakistan market\n\nonce again keeps the lead in pricing, \nalthough has cooled a touch since \nthe highs of August. \nThe Bangladesh market has steadily \nrebuilt appetite and is likely in a \nposition \nto \ncompete \nwith \nits \nneighbors in Gadani especially on \ntonnage coming from the East. \nWhile India remains well behind on \nconventional units the local buyers \ncontinues \nto \nabsorb \nspecialist"
  }
